<title>USA: Damark expands credit facility.</title>
<headline>Damark expands credit facility.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Damark International Inc, a mail order catalogue and membership company, said Thursday it has increased its overall credit facility to $50 million from $30 million.</p>
<p>The amended credit facility includes a $45 million sub-limit available for working capital and stand-by letter of credit requirements, the company said.</p>
<p>&quot;This expanded credit facility helps support our increased sales volume and allows for further growth of our business by providing additional working capital,&quot; Mark Cohn, Damark's chairman and chief executive officer, said in a news release.</p>
<p>Damark shares rose 3/8 to 15-1/8 Thursday.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
